<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!DOCTYPE refentry PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DocBook XML V4.2//EN"
   "http://www.oasis-open.org/docbook/xml/4.2/docbookx.dtd">
<refentry id="odfamountview">
  <refentryinfo>
    <productname>odfpy</productname>
    <author><firstname>Søren</firstname><surname>Roug</surname>
    <contrib>Original author</contrib>
    </author>
  </refentryinfo>
  <refmeta>
    <refentrytitle>odfamountview</refentrytitle>
    <manvolnum>1</manvolnum>
    <refmiscinfo class="manual">User commands</refmiscinfo>
  </refmeta>

<refnamediv>
<refname>odfamountview</refname>
<refpurpose>Show an amount column view of an OpenDocument spreadsheet</refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<cmdsynopsis>
    <command>odfamountview</command>
    <arg><option>-t <replaceable>table</replaceable></option></arg>
    <arg><option>-c <replaceable>column</replaceable></option></arg>
    <arg choice="plain"><replaceable>path</replaceable></arg>
</cmdsynopsis>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsect1><title>Description</title>
<para>
odfamountview reads a spreadsheet and reports, for every cell of a
monetary column, the value exactly as stored in the file, the currency,
and where the currency format comes from: an explicit cell style takes
precedence over the row default, which takes precedence over the column
default.  Cells that cannot be recognised as amounts are listed with the
reason, for example a cell that only displays a currency symbol as text
without storing a value.
</para>
<para>
Totals are computed per currency code, or per exact
(symbol, language, country) combination of the data style when no code
is stored.  Two currencies that happen to render the same symbol are
never added together, and every total lists the cell references and raw
values it was computed from so it can be traced back to the file.
</para>
</refsect1>
<refsect1><title>Options</title>
<variablelist>
  <varlistentry>
    <term>-t, --table</term>
    <listitem><para>Only inspect the named table.</para></listitem>
  </varlistentry>
  <varlistentry>
    <term>-c, --column</term>
    <listitem><para>Only inspect one column, given as a letter such as B.</para></listitem>
  </varlistentry>
</variablelist>
</refsect1>
<refsect1><title>Example</title>
<screen>
odfamountview sales.ods
</screen>
</refsect1>
</refentry>
